=== 2. LICENSE VERIFICATION (the geneva-notes lesson: explicit grant BEFORE ingest) ===
Verified in the pinned archive itself:
  - LICENSE: CC0 1.0 Universal public-domain dedication (full legalcode text, first line:
    'Creative Commons Legal Code / CC0 1.0 Universal'). Covers any compilation/formatting/
    markup rights in the digitization.
  - NOTICE: 'PUBLIC DOMAIN ... The underlying lexicon (Thayer, 1889) and the Strong's
    numbering (Strong, 1890) are ... in the public domain worldwide. This edition is a
    faithful digital reproduction ... dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0.'
  - Underlying work PD by age: Thayer d. 1901; corrected edition 1889 (manifest already
    asserts license='Public Domain', author_died=1901, year_written=1889).
  - ADR-008 forbidden-domain predicate run on the provenance hosts:
      github.com/EveryPromiseBible/Every-Promise-Thayers -> not forbidden
      everypromisebible.com                              -> not forbidden
  Caveat recorded: the NOTICE says the edition was 'decoded from a community digitization'
  without naming it. Accepted because (a) the 1889 text is PD regardless of digitizer,
  (b) the repo owner's CC0 dedication covers their compilation/markup rights, (c) neither
  host is a forbidden aggregator. Text-level artifacts of the classic digitization survive
  (fused words like 'Latinin-', inline 'STRONGS NT 2942a:' markers) — content, kept verbatim.

